# 0013. `/log`: read the thread in your editor

- Status: Proposed
- Date: 2026-11-25

Copying several lines out of the TUI picks up pane borders, side panes and wrap breaks,
because terminal copy works on screen cells. `/log` opens the thread's text in the user's
editor instead, from a temp file that is deleted when the editor closes.

## Technical details
- **Command** (ADR 0008 table, `commands::COMMANDS` + `App::command`):
  - `/log`: the whole current thread. `/log <n>`: the last `n` messages.
  - Empty thread: "nothing to log yet", no file.
- **Source**: the thread's `events.jsonl` (ADR 0010), never the screen. Already redacted by
  `Runtime::record`, so the file carries no key values.
- **Format**: Markdown, `.md` suffix, lines not wrapped:
  ```
  # <thread title> · <date>

  ## you · 19:41
  @codex review this

  ## codex · 19:42
  <reply, verbatim>

  > claude → codex (ask) · 1.2k tokens
  > <exact prompt>
  >
  > <reply>
  ```
  - Messages verbatim; `ask` exchanges in full as quotes (the user wants to read them);
    tool calls one line each (`[tool: edit src/app.rs]`); errors and status lines as `> !`.
  - A pure function `log::render(&[EventLine], last: Option<usize>) -> String` in the
    library, covered by insta snapshots.
- **State/IO split** (ADR 0002): `App::update` returns `Effect::OpenLog { last }`; the loop
  reads the transcript, renders, writes the file, runs the editor.
- **Editor**: `$VISUAL`, then `$EDITOR`, then `nvim`; split with shell-words (`nvim -p` works).
  For `nvim`/`vim`, add `-R` (read-only: yank works, edits are pointless because the file is
  deleted). Not found / non-zero exit: error line in the chat, file deleted.
- **How it opens**:
  - Inside tmux (`$TMUX` set): `tmux display-popup -E -w 90% -h 90% '<editor> <path>'`,
    spawned as a child process. Roundtable keeps running and drawing underneath; nothing
    is suspended. The command string is shell-quoted (the data dir has a space:
    `Application Support`).
  - Outside tmux: suspend. Stop the terminal-input task (else it steals nvim's keys), leave
    the alternate screen, disable raw mode, run the editor and wait, then restore and force a
    full redraw. Streams and asks keep arriving and update `App` meanwhile; only drawing
    pauses.
  - One `/log` at a time: a second one while the editor is open says so.
- **Temp file**: `<data_root>/tmp/` (0700, like `threads/`), file `<title-slug>-<ulid>.md`,
  created `create_new`, mode 0600. Deleted when the editor process exits, whatever the exit
  code. Startup sweeps `tmp/` for leftovers from a crash.
- **Snapshot**: the file is the thread at the moment of `/log`; new messages aren't added.
- **Consequences**: copy, search and reading back use the user's own editor and keys; no
  in-TUI selection or mouse capture needed, so tmux mouse/copy mode stays as is. Costs: a
  render format to maintain next to the TUI's, and the suspend path's terminal handoff.

## Technologies and alternatives
- Involved: tmux `display-popup` (tmux ≥ 3.2), crossterm (raw mode, alternate screen),
  `shell-words`, ulid, insta.
- Alternatives:
  - `/copy [n]` to the clipboard: copies whole messages only, no partial selection.
  - In-TUI selection with mouse capture: breaks tmux mouse selection over the pane.
  - `/export` to a kept file: leaves transcript copies around; can come later on the same render.
  - Live view (`tail -f` style): later; a snapshot covers copying and reading back.
